WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:18.175
The next morning, Katie and Joy hurried to the fourth-grade classroom.

2
00:00:18.176 --> 00:00:22.166
They slid into their seats just as the bell rang.

3
00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.874
Katie looked to her right.

4
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:25.805
Luke was whispering.

5
00:00:25.806 --> 00:00:27.707
Olivia was laughing.

6
00:00:27.708 --> 00:00:30.506
Katie rolled her eyes.

7
00:00:30.507 --> 00:00:34.641
"Okay, boys and girls," said Ms. Barrow.

8
00:00:34.642 --> 00:00:37.768
"Take out your pencils and notebooks.

9
00:00:37.769 --> 00:00:39.259
Let's get to work.

10
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.910
Here are your fourth-grade math books!"

11
00:00:42.911 --> 00:00:45.841
Carlos looked down at the cover of his book.

12
00:00:45.842 --> 00:00:50.647
He saw a disk that was cut into eight equal pieces.

13
00:00:50.648 --> 00:00:56.745
"I know what this picture means!" he groaned. "More fractions!"

14
00:00:56.746 --> 00:01:01.455
"No fractions today, Carlos," said Ms. Barrow.

15
00:01:01.456 --> 00:01:10.331
"Today we will review whole numbers—big whole numbers—and study counting in tens.

16
00:01:10.332 --> 00:01:13.156
We may get to a million!"

17
00:01:13.157 --> 00:01:15.350
After math came science.

18
00:01:15.351 --> 00:01:20.240
Ms. Barrow gave each student a book called Amphibians.

19
00:01:20.241 --> 00:01:23.197
Olivia pointed to the frog on the cover.

20
00:01:23.198 --> 00:01:26.570
"This looks like a green-and-black poison dart frog!

21
00:01:26.571 --> 00:01:30.000
They live in Hawaii!" she said.

22
00:01:30.001 --> 00:01:32.653
"Smarty-pants," thought Katie.

23
00:01:32.654 --> 00:01:35.517
She flipped through the book.

24
00:01:35.518 --> 00:01:38.404
"Where are the turtles?" she called out.

25
00:01:38.405 --> 00:01:42.906
"A three-toed box turtle lives right in our backyard."

26
00:01:42.907 --> 00:01:46.154
"That's interesting," said Ms. Barrow.

27
00:01:46.155 --> 00:01:49.480
"But turtles are not amphibians, Katie.

28
00:01:49.481 --> 00:01:52.765
Turtles are reptiles."

29
00:01:52.766 --> 00:01:55.406
Katie's face turned bright red.

30
00:01:55.407 --> 00:01:58.491
"Oops," she said.

31
00:01:58.492 --> 00:02:03.818
After science Ms. Barrow announced the start of a special health project.

32
00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:08.710
"Now is the time to form healthy habits," she said.

33
00:02:08.711 --> 00:02:14.992
"When you take good care of yourself, you feel good—and you may live longer too."

34
00:02:14.993 --> 00:02:19.926
Ms. Barrow gave everyone a book called Be Healthy!

35
00:02:19.927 --> 00:02:26.321
"Next week each of you will give a report to the class," the teacher went on.

36
00:02:26.322 --> 00:02:30.674
"You will tell us about one topic in this book.

37
00:02:30.675 --> 00:02:36.817
And I want you to use your imagination to make your report interesting and fun."

38
00:02:36.818 --> 00:02:43.341
Then she asked each student to pull a slip of paper from a box.

39
00:02:43.342 --> 00:02:45.105
Olivia was first.

40
00:02:45.106 --> 00:02:46.873
She opened her paper.

41
00:02:46.874 --> 00:02:49.261
"Healthy Skin," she read.

42
00:02:49.262 --> 00:02:51.459
Laura drew Healthy Eyes.

43
00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.919
Luke got Nutrition.

44
00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.325
Carlos unfolded his paper.

45
00:02:56.326 --> 00:02:59.352
"Healthy Ears," he said.

46
00:02:59.353 --> 00:03:04.173
"What? I can't hear you?" said Katie. Nobody laughed.

47
00:03:04.174 --> 00:03:07.523
She looked around. "Get it?"

48
00:03:07.524 --> 00:03:10.650
"We get it," said Carlos.

49
00:03:10.651 --> 00:03:12.917
Larry got Sports Safety.

50
00:03:12.918 --> 00:03:15.914
Then someone pulled out Sleep and Rest.

51
00:03:15.915 --> 00:03:17.885
Next it was Katie's turn.

52
00:03:17.886 --> 00:03:20.501
She reached into the box.

53
00:03:20.502 --> 00:03:23.132
"Exercise," she read.

54
00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:27.454
"Hey, that's the same as playing, isn't it?"

55
00:03:27.455 --> 00:03:34.397
Ms. Barrow smiled. "Some people think of it that way. Yes, Katie."

56
00:03:34.398 --> 00:03:36.693
Finally it was Joy's turn.

57
00:03:36.694 --> 00:03:41.732
"Building Friendships?" she said. "Is this a health topic?"

58
00:03:41.733 --> 00:03:44.360
"Yes," said Ms. Barrow.

59
00:03:44.361 --> 00:03:47.315
"Friends help us feel good about ourselves.

60
00:03:47.316 --> 00:03:51.484
That's a very important part of being healthy."

61
00:03:51.485 --> 00:03:53.266
"Okay," said Joy.

62
00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:54.836
She liked her topic.

63
00:03:54.837 --> 00:03:58.452
It would be fun to do a report on friendship.

64
00:03:58.453 --> 00:04:02.780
"That's all for today, boys and girls," said Ms. Barrow.

65
00:04:02.781 --> 00:04:06.079
"Please clean up before the bell rings."

66
00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.352
Soon the fourth graders were rushing out of the building.

67
00:04:10.353 --> 00:04:13.531
"Not a bad day," said Katie to Joy.

68
00:04:13.532 --> 00:04:16.814
"Both of our health topics sound fun."

69
00:04:16.815 --> 00:04:22.038
Then Katie heard Luke speaking in a high, squeaky voice.

70
00:04:22.039 --> 00:04:26.002
"Ms. Barrow, where are the turtles?"

71
00:04:26.003 --> 00:04:30.910
All the fourth graders laughed—except Katie.

72
00:04:30.911 --> 00:04:34.415
"That's not funny, Luke!" she said.

73
00:04:34.416 --> 00:04:39.068
Some kids tried to stop laughing, but they couldn't.

74
00:04:39.069 --> 00:04:42.625
"He's only teasing, Katie," said Joy.

75
00:04:42.626 --> 00:04:47.389
"Don't be mad," said Luke. "Hey! I've got an idea.

76
00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.438
Let's all go to Fried Pie Heaven."

77
00:04:50.439 --> 00:04:53.486
But Katie was still angry at her cousin.

78
00:04:53.487 --> 00:04:57.652
"With you? No thanks!" she said.

79
00:04:57.653 --> 00:05:02.095
Then she got on her bike and sped down School Street.

80
00:05:02.096 --> 00:05:05.700
"I think she's upset," said Carlos.

81
00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:09.129
"I know she's upset," said Joy.

82
00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:12.811
"I've never heard of fried pies," said Olivia.

83
00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.937
"What are they?"

84
00:05:14.938 --> 00:05:17.306
Everyone smiled.

85
00:05:17.307 --> 00:05:21.248
"Fried pies are sweet!" said Laura.

86
00:05:21.249 --> 00:05:24.865
"Fried pies are fruity!" said Joy.

87
00:05:24.866 --> 00:05:29.982
"And Luke's mom makes the best ones in town!" said Carlos.

88
00:05:29.983 --> 00:05:32.496
"Race you there!" Luke said.

89
00:05:32.497 --> 00:05:37.494
"On your mark, get set, go!"
